{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2972,"ns":0,"title":"Abstraction","extract":"Abstraction is the process of generalizing rules and concepts from specific examples, literal (real or concrete) signifiers, first principles, or other methods. The result of the process, an abstraction, is a concept that acts as a common noun for all subordinate concepts and connects any related concepts as a group, field or category.","description":"Process of generalization","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}